# Project 07: AWS Application Load Balancer (ALB) & High Availability Setup

## 📌 Architecture Overview
This project demonstrates a multi-AZ, fault-tolerant, and auto-scaling web application deployment on AWS using custom VPC networking and an Application Load Balancer (ALB).

## 🏗️ Architecture Components
- **Custom VPC:** 2 Public Subnets across multiple Availability Zones (`ap-south-1a`, `ap-south-1b`).
- **Internet Gateway & Route Tables:** Configured for public internet routing.
- **Security Groups:** 
  - `ALB-SG`: Restricts inbound traffic on Port 80 to public internet (`0.0.0.0/0`).
  - `EC2-SG`: Restricts inbound HTTP traffic strictly to traffic coming from ALB.
- **Target Group (`TG-Project07`):** Health check enabled for HTTP traffic.
- **Application Load Balancer (`ALB-Project07`):** Multi-AZ internet-facing load balancer routing traffic to healthy EC2 instances.
- **Auto Scaling Group (`web-server-asg`):** Maintains high availability and automatically launches/terminates instances based on workload demand.

